---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="For Farmers" description="We buy paddy straw, Napier grass, and cattle dung. We pay within 14 days. By bank transfer. Within 50 km of Thatipadu.">
  <Section eyebrow="For Farmers" title="We buy what you would have burned.">
    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-[1.2fr_1fr] gap-10 items-start">
      <div class="prose-svge">
        <p class="text-xl leading-relaxed">
          If you farm within 50&nbsp;km of Thatipadu village in Vizianagaram or Srikakulam district — we want to talk to you.
        </p>
        <p>
          We are building a Compressed Bio-Gas plant that needs daily feedstock. We pay per tonne, on the supply slip, into your bank account, within 14 days. Every time.
        </p>

        <h2>What we buy</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Paddy straw</strong> — dry, baled or loose, post-harvest. Standard rate per tonne.</li>
          <li><strong>Napier grass</strong> — under a contract-farming agreement on your land or ours.</li>
          <li><strong>Cattle dung</strong> — fresh, in volume, from your shed.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What you get back</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>A second income</strong> — cash for the residue you would have burned or wasted.</li>
          <li><strong>Fermented Organic Manure</strong> — at a fair rate, returned to your fields if you want it. Better for soil than chemical fertilizer.</li>
          <li><strong>14-day payment</strong> — bank transfer to your account. No "next week", no arrears.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How it works</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>You contact us by email, WhatsApp (when published), or in person once construction begins.</li>
          <li>We agree a rate and quantity, in writing, in plain Telugu or English.</li>
          <li>You deliver to the plant or our pickup point.</li>
          <li>You sign a supply slip. We pay against the slip.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What we are NOT</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>A government subsidy scheme. We pay a market rate from our own budget.</li>
          <li>A long-term lock-in. No bonded labour, no "you must supply 100% to us" clauses.</li>
          <li>A late-paying middleman. Our books are audited; payments are tracked monthly.</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="mt-8">
          <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary">Email us ↗</a>
          <span class="ml-3 text-sm font-mono text-[color:var(--color-slate-2)]">A Telugu page is in the works for 2026 Q3.</span>
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="space-y-5">
        <div class="rounded-2xl bg-[color:var(--color-forest)] text-[color:var(--color-paper)] p-6">
          <div class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest opacity-80">Our promise</div>
          <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-snug">14-day payment. Every supply slip. Every time.</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-xs opacity-90">No 60-day arrears. No "next week" delays. Bank transfer only.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl bg-[color:var(--color-paper-2)] p-6 text-sm">
          <div class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-[color:var(--color-saffron-text)]">Where</div>
          <p class="mt-2">Plant site: <strong>Thatipadu village</strong>, Regidi Amadalavalasa mandal, Vizianagaram district, AP — 532440.</p>
          <p class="mt-2">Service radius: <strong>50&nbsp;km</strong> — covers most of Vizianagaram and Srikakulam districts.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl bg-[color:var(--color-paper-2)] p-6 text-sm">
          <div class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-[color:var(--color-saffron-text)]">What we won't pay</div>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-[color:var(--color-slate)]">
            <li>Wet or rotting straw — must be dry and clean.</li>
            <li>Plastic-contaminated bales.</li>
            <li>Pre-burned or charred residue (defeats the point).</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Common questions" title="What farmers ask us first" narrow>
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <details class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-black/5 p-5 open:bg-[color:var(--color-paper-2)]">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-forest)]">Do I have to sign a long-term contract?</summary>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">No. For paddy straw, every supply is on its own slip. For Napier grass, we offer a season-long contract because we want to know we'll have feedstock — but it's renewable per season, never multi-year-locked. There is no "bonded supply" anywhere in this model.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-black/5 p-5 open:bg-[color:var(--color-paper-2)]">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-forest)]">How do I know you'll actually pay in 14 days?</summary>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">Every payment is bank-transfer against a numbered supply slip you keep a copy of. From the day concrete is poured, we will publish farmer-payments-made as one of the monthly numbers on <a href="/news/">/news/</a>. If we ever miss a 14-day window, you'll see it in the public log first.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-black/5 p-5 open:bg-[color:var(--color-paper-2)]">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-forest)]">What if my paddy straw is wet from rain?</summary>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">We don't pay for wet straw — it kills the digester economics. But: if a forecast tells you the rain is coming, call us before harvest. We have flexibility on timing. We do not have flexibility on moisture content at the gate.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-black/5 p-5 open:bg-[color:var(--color-paper-2)]">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-forest)]">Do I get the Fermented Organic Manure for free, or do I pay?</summary>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">FOM is sold back at a fair market rate — significantly below chemical fertilizer for the equivalent nutrient load. We are not a charity, but we are also not pricing FOM as a profit centre. The model is: gas pays the bills; FOM rebuilds the catchment we source from.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-black/5 p-5 open:bg-[color:var(--color-paper-2)]">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-forest)]">Will Napier grass work on my land?</summary>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">Napier handles most coastal-Andhra soils, including stony or low-water plots that struggle with paddy. We will visit your land before signing — at our cost — to confirm. There is no application fee.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-black/5 p-5 open:bg-[color:var(--color-paper-2)]">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-forest)]">When does this actually start?</summary>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">The plant is in pre-construction today. Once construction begins, we will publish a target month for first feedstock collection — likely around the commissioning date or just before. Email us now to be on the contact list when that happens.</p>
      </details>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm">
      Couldn't find your question? Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}?subject=Farmer%20enquiry`}>{SITE.email}</a> with subject line "Farmer enquiry".
    </p>
  </Section>
</Base>
